From b1dc55900fbc27ce06f2616ddeee841e9dd8b6f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 13:36:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] i686: (a) alloca-precise hazard scan, (b) direct phys-reg
 materialization

Follow-up work on the ecx/edx caller-saved allocation, attacking the
accumulator-detour bloat from three sides:

(a) Hazard scan precision: 32-bit loads/stores whose pointer is a
    NON-over-aligned alloca resolve to SlotAddr::Direct and emit
    acc-only code (movl slot,%eax / movl %eax,slot) -- no %ecx pointer
    staging. The scan now whitelists those (align <= 16, mirroring
    slot_assignment.rs; %gs:/%fs: seg_override stays fail-closed),
    extending ecx/edx live-range viability across alloca traffic.

(b) Direct materialization: new trait hook emit_load_direct_to_phys_reg
    with an i686 override -- `movl slot,%ecx` / `movl $imm,%edx` /
    `leal slot,%ecx` in ONE instruction where emit_copy_value's default
    detoured through movl-to-%eax + movl %eax,%dest. Wide values and
    over-aligned allocas correctly refuse (fall back to acc path).
    Also applied inside 32-bit Select arms, where the load+move pair
    sits immediately before a label and no peephole can ever prove
    deadness across that barrier.

    New peephole Pattern 2b catches the remaining textual shape
    `movl $X,%eax; movl %eax,%REG` -> `movl $X,%REG` under the same
    bounded deadness scan as Pattern 2a (no memory operands, so no
    slot-bias interaction).

Kernel repro szt.c -Os -m32: 1833 -> 1829. Correctness unchanged
everywhere else.

Validation: cargo test 699; regression 283; correctness 50; linker 91;
intrinsics 3; asm-diff exact; m32 differential fuzz 450/450 (seeds
0:150, O0+O2+Os); x86-64 fuzz 300/300 (O2+Os); runtime reproducers
mulhaz/gep0/fptest all exit 0.
